WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.738
Now how to deliver it,
starting with the estate.

2
00:00:02.738 --> 00:00:06.260
You can't modernize what you haven't
enumerated, and nothing can be

3
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.175
retired until someone has written
down everything it was quietly doing.

4
00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:15.001
Ask what's in a long-lived forest and the
honest answer is usually more than anyone

5
00:00:15.001 --> 00:00:18.098
on the current team knows:
trusts no one can fully map,

6
00:00:18.098 --> 00:00:20.763
Group Policy whose
authors left a decade ago,

7
00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:25.372
certificate templates whose permissions
open privilege-escalation paths,

8
00:00:25.372 --> 00:00:29.550
and servers past support, each of
which needs a disposition in the plan.

9
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.800
The assessment follows three rules.

10
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.287
It's read-only, enforced in the
account, the code and the audit trail.

11
00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:41.027
It's least-privilege: never a domain
or enterprise admin, starting from

12
00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:46.338
default read rights and adding only
narrow, recorded additions, never secrets.

13
00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:50.231
And every run carries
provenance: who ran it, when,

14
00:00:50.231 --> 00:00:54.612
against what, with which rights,
and a hash of every file.

15
00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:56.862
The engine rejects a run without it.

16
00:00:56.862 --> 00:01:00.294
The output maps privileged
groups and service accounts,

17
00:01:00.294 --> 00:01:03.287
so it's stored encrypted
and handled as sensitive.

18
00:01:03.287 --> 00:01:06.916
And because broad enumeration
looks like reconnaissance,

19
00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:09.063
security operations is told first.

20
00:01:09.063 --> 00:01:12.715
One more input decides whether
an application may move:

21
00:01:12.715 --> 00:01:16.924
how many round trips it makes to
its data, measured, not estimated.

22
00:01:16.924 --> 00:01:19.387
The steward commissions it in Phase 0.

23
00:01:19.387 --> 00:01:23.567
In the program's experience a first
pass takes days to a few weeks,

24
00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.610
and Gate G0 needs it committed.
